# Map Control Tab Scope

You are in the **Map Control** tab. Your responsibility is limited to map-related systems.

## You OWN and may freely change
- `Assets/Scripts/Core/MapController.cs`
- `Assets/Scripts/Map/` (MapZone, EnvironmentalResourceSpawner, MAP_CONTROL_SCOPE.md)

## You do NOT own (other tabs)
- **Loot/drops**: LootManager, ResourcePickup, drop rates, RollEnemyLoot
- **Monster spawn**: Enemy spawning, waves, spawn points
- **Player**: PlayerController, input
- **Health**: HealthSystem, toxic gas formula, healing, death flow
- **Towers/combat**: Tower, aggro, combat

When changes require touching those areas, only add minimal integration (e.g. call an existing API or read a value). Do not refactor or redesign logic inside those modules. Prefer suggesting "have the Loot/Enemy/Player/Health tab do X" when the change belongs there.

Reference: `Assets/Scripts/Map/MAP_CONTROL_SCOPE.md` for full scope and boundaries.
